.TH TTYCHATTER.MAILBOT 1 "May 2026" "ttychatter.mailbot 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ttychatter.mailbot \- email transport adapter and remote control surface for ttychatter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ttychatter.mailbot
[--config-file PATH] [--once|--daemon|--dry-run] [--doctor] [--list-candidates]
.PP
.B ttychatter.mailbot
[--config|--raw-config] [--sessions|--list-sessions] [--manpage] [--update-models]
.PP
.B ttychatter.mailbot
[--set KEY VALUE] [--unset KEY] [--set-imap-password [--gpg]] [--set-smtp-password [--gpg]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
ttychatter.mailbot reads unread IMAP mail, accepts only messages from ALLOWED_FROM,
extracts a subject token, and either sends the message body to ttychatter.python
or handles a local mailbot control command. Replies are sent by sendmail or SMTP.
.PP
The 0.4 command grammar reserves braces for ttychatter chat sessions and uses
bare subjects for mailbot controls.
.SH CHAT SUBJECTS
Ordinary chat subjects use this form:
.PP
.B tc:{session-name}
.PP
The special chat subject
.PP
.B tc:{new}
.PP
starts a new unnamed chat from the mailbot side. The mailbot passes no session
argument to ttychatter.python, so ttychatter.python creates its normal
session-YYYY-MM-DD-HH-MM-SS log name.
.SH CONTROL SUBJECTS
The preferred control forms are:
.PP
.B tc:CONFIG
.PP
export or apply the mailbot config attachment.
.PP
.B tc:MODELS
.PP
run ttychatter.python --update-models and attach the resulting models-cache.json.
.PP
.B tc:CMD
.PP
run the first nonempty message-body line as a mailbot command.
.PP
.B tc:command args
.PP
run a mailbot command directly from the subject.
.PP
Legacy subjects tc:{CONFIG}, tc:{MAILBOT},
and tc:{MAILBOT:command args} remain accepted for compatibility,
but new mail should use the bare control subjects.
.SH SUPPORTED COMMANDS
.TP
.B help
Return the email command summary. Example subject: tc:help.
.TP
.B manpage
Return the configured external manpage as an email attachment when found,
otherwise return the embedded fallback. Aliases: manual, get-manpage, fetch-manpage.
.TP
.B sessions
List saved session names with short head and tail previews from each session log.
.TP
.B search TEXT
Search all session logs for TEXT. If the subject is only tc:search,
the first nonempty body line supplies TEXT.
.TP
.B search-session SESSION TEXT
Search a single session log for TEXT.
.TP
.B rename-session OLD NEW
Rename a session log after sanitizing both names.
.TP
.B update-models
Run ttychatter.python --update-models, then attach the resulting models-cache.json
when the cache file is present and smaller than MAX_OUTGOING_ATTACHMENT_BYTES.
The subject tc:MODELS is the preferred shorthand.
.TP
.B model-list [FLAGS]
Run ttychatter.python --models. Aliases: models, list-models, models-list, show-models. The safe model-list flags are
--all, --sort VALUE, --modellist-sort-tokens, --min-input-tokens N,
--min-output-tokens N, --hide-preview, --show-preview, --require-tokens,
--allow-missing-tokens, and --model-type VALUE.
.TP
.B routers [FLAGS]
Run ttychatter.python --routers with the same safe model-list flags.
.TP
.B favorites
Return ttychatter's model favorites.
.TP
.B favorite-model MODEL
Add MODEL to ttychatter's favorites file.
.TP
.B unfavorite-model MODEL
Remove MODEL from ttychatter's favorites file.
.TP
.B test-model MODEL
Run ttychatter.python --test-model MODEL.
.TP
.B ttyconfig
Return ttychatter.python --config output.
.TP
.B ttydoctor
Return ttychatter.python --doctor diagnostics.
.TP
.B show-memory SESSION
Return ttychatter's memory snapshot for SESSION.
.TP
.B clear-memory SESSION
Clear ttychatter's memory snapshot for SESSION.
.TP
.B tty-set KEY VALUE
Run ttychatter.python --set KEY VALUE. Do not send secrets by email.
.TP
.B tty-unset KEY
Run ttychatter.python --unset KEY.
.TP
.B credits
Return ttychatter.python --credits output.
.SH LOCAL CONFIG OUTPUT
The local --config command prints the parsed effective config, not a byte-for-byte
copy of the config file. It includes PROCESS_USER, HOME,
TTYCHATTER_MAILBOT_CONFIG, XDG_CONFIG_HOME, CONFIG_FILE, CONFIG_EXISTS,
CONFIG_READABLE, and CONFIG_MODE to make wrong-user and wrong-path mistakes
visible. Unknown keys and comments are not shown there; use --raw-config to
print the actual config file with plaintext password lines redacted. The
default config path is TTYCHATTER_MAILBOT_CONFIG, then
XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ttychatter/mailbot/config, then ~/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/config;
--config-file PATH has final precedence.
.SH CONFIG COMMAND
The subject
.PP
.B tc:CONFIG
.PP
exports the mailbot config as an attachment. Reply with an edited config
attachment using the same subject to replace the config; a timestamped backup is kept.
Plaintext IMAP_PASSWORD and SMTP_PASSWORD values are redacted on export.
.SH CONFIGURATION KEYS
Core keys include IMAP_HOST, IMAP_PORT, IMAP_SSL, IMAP_USER, IMAP_PASSWORD,
IMAP_PASSWORD_GPG_FILE, SEND_METHOD, SENDMAIL_PATH, SMTP_HOST, SMTP_PORT,
SMTP_SSL, SMTP_STARTTLS, SMTP_USER, SMTP_PASSWORD, SMTP_PASSWORD_GPG_FILE,
MAIL_FROM, MAIL_TO, ALLOWED_FROM, SUBJECT_PREFIX, CONFIG_SUBJECT_TOKEN,
MODELS_SUBJECT_TOKEN, COMMAND_SUBJECT_TOKEN, MAILBOT_SUBJECT_TOKEN,
POLL_INTERVAL, MAX_MESSAGES_PER_RUN, MAX_BODY_BYTES, MAX_ATTACHMENT_BYTES,
PROCESS_ATTACHMENTS, MARK_SEEN, TTYCHATTER_COMMAND, TTYCHATTER_EXTRA_ARGS,
TTYCHATTER_CONTROL_TIMEOUT, MAILBOT_MANPAGE_FILE, SESSION_DIR, ATTACHMENT_DIR,
MODEL_CACHE_FILE, WORK_DIR, PROCESSED_DB, SESSION_LIST_HEAD_LINES,
SESSION_LIST_TAIL_LINES, SESSION_LIST_MAX_SESSIONS, SESSION_PREVIEW_LINE_CHARS,
SESSION_SEARCH_MAX_MATCHES, MAX_COMMAND_OUTPUT_BYTES, MAX_OUTGOING_ATTACHMENT_BYTES,
REPLY_SUBJECT_PREFIX, and INCLUDE_TTYCHATTER_STDERR.
.SH SECURITY
ALLOWED_FROM is required. The mailbot should use a private mailbox and a distinct
MAIL_FROM address where practical. Commands are not shell-expanded, but email is
not a good channel for secrets; use the local --set-imap-password and
--set-smtp-password commands for passwords.
.SH GPG PASSWORD FILES
With --gpg, the mailbot stores IMAP and SMTP passwords in external gpg files and
decrypts them with gpg --quiet --decrypt at runtime. Version 0.3.1 passes GPG_TTY
automatically to gpg when the mailbot has a controlling terminal, trims trailing
CR/LF from decrypted password files, and prints process user, HOME, and GPG_TTY
in gpg-agent diagnostics. For interactive tests, also set export GPG_TTY=$(tty)
and test the password file directly with gpg --decrypt as the mailbot user.
Do not diagnose this by switching to root unless the service is actually
configured to run as root; root changes HOME, GNUPGHOME, and the gpg-agent socket
and may load a different config. Unattended daemon, cron, rc, or systemd launches
need gpg-agent to have the passphrase already cached, or should use a mode-0600
plaintext password line or SEND_METHOD=sendmail where appropriate.
.SH IMAP LOGIN DIAGNOSTICS
Version 0.3.1 rejects empty IMAP_USER, empty IMAP password, and CR/LF in IMAP
login values before sending LOGIN. A server reply such as LOGIN command error:
BAD usually means the command syntax was invalid, commonly due to an empty user,
a password with carriage return/newline, or running with a different user/HOME
than the configured mailbot account. Use --config and --doctor to confirm the
loaded config and process user.
.SH MANPAGE LOOKUP
The email manpage command and the local --manpage command use the first readable
manpage found.  The lookup order is TTYCHATTER_MAILBOT_MANPAGE_FILE when
set, otherwise MAILBOT_MANPAGE_FILE, then ~/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/ttychatter.mailbot.1,
the directory beside the script, the directory beside argv[0], XDG/user man1
directories, system man1 directories, then the current working directory.
Matching .1.gz files are accepted. If no external file is found, the embedded
fallback is used.
.SH FILES
Default config: ~/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/config
.PP
Config path environment override: TTYCHATTER_MAILBOT_CONFIG
.PP
Preferred local manpage: ~/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/ttychatter.mailbot.1
.PP
Alternate user manpage: ~/.local/share/man/man1/ttychatter.mailbot.1
.PP
System manpage: /usr/local/share/man/man1/ttychatter.mailbot.1
.PP
Default processed-message database: ~/.local/state/ttychatter/mailbot/processed-ids.txt
.PP
Default session directory: ~/.local/share/ttychatter/openrouter/sessions
.PP
Default model cache: ~/.config/ttychatter/openrouter/models-cache.json
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 indicates success. Nonzero status indicates configuration, IMAP, SMTP,
sendmail, or ttychatter subprocess failure.
